{
  "id": 210644471,
  "iid": 10027,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Include subfilters in tshark SRT tables",
  "description": "When printing SRT filters, tshark currently only shows the filter registered\nby the dissector with init_srt_table(), e.g. \"smb2.cmd\" or \"nfs.procedure_V3\".\n\nThe subfilter is useful information to have when reviewing output,\nparticularly when the same table is repeated with different filters (e.g.\n\"tshark -z smb2,srt,ip==192.0.2.1 -z smb2,srt,ip==192.0.2.2\") where it is not\nobvious which table is which (and more so if you are not aware that the tables\nare printed in reverse order).\n\nWith the patch, the subfilter is added in parenthesis, e.g.:\n\n```\n$ tshark -q -r nfsv3.pcap.gz -z \"rpc,srt,100003,3,udp.port==3298\"\n\n===================================================================\nRPC SRT Statistics:\nFilter: nfs.procedure_v3 and (udp.port==3298)\nIndex  Procedure              Calls    Min SRT    Max SRT    Avg SRT    Sum SRT\n    0  NULL                        1   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000\n==================================================================\n```",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-03-12T11:48:50.454Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-03-23T10:09:07.236Z",
